Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

T-505 (the owner's "cheaper part pictures", 2026-11-03). A frame without its parts (flag 128) used to carry
one signature of all its parts; when it moved, the parts pass composed and read every part. Now each rect of
the parts list has a signature of its own: the outermost fixed or sticky layer's subtree as before, every
subtree layer's last paint as the stamp of one counter that only goes up (CompositableTransactionParent stamps
each compositable update's layer, part or not: a layer that becomes a part later carries it — review F2), the
part's scale and the sub-pixel phase of its position, where it sits inside the rect and its size (review F3: a
part wider than the frame moving sideways, or moving inside a merged rect, keeps the rect's size), and the
rect's size; a rect no part's rect meets (a nested part's own) takes every part's with its index and place
(review F6). The whole signature is the rects' and the global paint count, so a daemon with the one signature
behaves as before (every part read when any moved).

jihad_offscreen_compose_post3/start3 (jihad_offscreen_overview_ok answers 4) take the list of signatures the
daemon holds pictures of; the pass packs and reads only the rects whose signature is not in it, in rect order,
and the poll's 54 ints carry each rect's signature (49..52) and the rects read as a mask (53). post2/start2
keep their meaning.

Measured by finger on desktop Wikipedia (its two sidebars; the contents panel, 310 of 340 KB, is the one that
changes): the pass reads the panel alone, 10.4 -> 11.4 fps flowing; the long page unchanged. Verify 0 wrong
rows over the scripted pans on both (docs/rounds/t505-2026-11-03/notes.txt).

